00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:24,480
The holophonics technique is unique because highest quality sound with full spatial effect can be recorded without the use of traditional microphones.

104
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:34,720
The technology is based on a new understanding of the physiology of human hearing, and this new knowledge is utilized in the recording process.

105
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:51,200
Holophonics is based on the hypothesis that we do not perceive sound in a passive manner, with the sound waves impacting our eardrums and our brain, computing characteristics and location from the frequency, intensity, and arrival time at each ear.

106
00:11:51,200 --> 00:12:04,800
Instead, the technology is based on the premise that the human ear generates its own reference tone, which interferes with incoming sounds to create the necessary spatial information for analysis by the brain.

107
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:28,880
Like laser beam shining through a hologram, it decodes, reproducing the original ambient conditions.

108
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:47,400
Consider the sphere of human oral perception as being divided into millions of minute points of awareness, and think of these points as all being different color, with each color relating to a different position that the brain could instantly identify through reception of the colors.

109
00:12:47,400 --> 00:13:01,480
The hue of sounds coming from behind the listener would differ from the sounds arriving in front, and the brain can then perceive direction independent of intensity or phase information.

110
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:06,920
The holophonics technology replicates this new definition of the hearing process.

111
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:13,400
Holophonics recordings are based in the interaction between the sound of reality and the reference tone.

112
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:22,120
A listening device has been developed which encodes spatial information resulting from the encounter of the reference tone with incoming sounds.

113
00:13:22,120 --> 00:13:29,640
These interference patterns represent accurate spatial information as well as the incoming sound itself.

114
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:40,440
It's actually named Ringo.

115
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:48,840
To record, Ringo is placed in the desired position and connected to a standard recording or broadcasting system.

116
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:58,520
The listener will hear the sounds which reach Ringo from a 360 degree sphere with accurate depth and spatial information.

117
00:13:58,520 --> 00:14:03,240
Again, Ringo does not contain traditional microphones.

118
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:13,800
Instead, the unique design and ability to generate an appropriate reference tone provides the basis for recording or broadcasting the captured auditory information.

119
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:21,440
For the listener, this method of recording does for the ears what holographic pictures does for the eyes.

120
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:23,760
It is three-dimensional reality.

121
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:36,080
Ringo replaces microphones in the recording of broadcast chains and can be connected to any common recording or broadcasting equipment with optimal results obtained through digital technology.

122
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:46,800
Playback or broadcast is possible over headphones or any existing mono or stereo speaker system with various levels of spatial effect.

123
00:14:46,800 --> 00:15:02,320
Optimal effects occur when two tracks, stereo, are played utilizing digital technology over headphones, and minimal effects when played over a single mono speaker.

